  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Projeto Crescer para a Paz ( growth towards peace)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enable children, adolescents, young people and their families to grow and develop in a culture of long-lasting peace in two violent urban favelas (shanty towns) in North East Brazil. The project is implemented by two local Brazilian organisations, GCASC and Galpao, based in Olinda and Recife. 

The &#x201C;Growing towards Peace&#x201D; project aims to address the problems of social violence, vulnerability and marginalisation of children and young people, through five key strategic lines of work: 
1) workshops with at risk children and adolescents on citizenship, the arts and culture, healthcare, parenthood and literacy and psycho-social support; 
2) vocational training and workshops on issues affecting young people, supporting them to become &#x2018;multiplying agents (community activists); 3) engaging with the parents in meetings, home visits, community activities, cultural events and specific workshops and activities, such as the family group, women groups and Dad&#x2019;s football. 
4) community lobbying and advocacy actions aimed at improving the community, and working with schools and health posts, to unify the community.
5) facilitating strategic planning, fundraising support and developing policies and procedures to ensure the organisations are accountable to their stakeholders, and strengthen the institutional capacity of the two organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
